{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And he will leave his father and die.</b> The lad will die on the way, because he is pampered and tender and has not been tested so that a wayfarer should come upon him on foot. It further includes that his father too will die from grief over his son, and this comes to teach that the life of the father is bound up with the life of the lad; and so he explained afterward, that since the soul of Jacob is bound to the soul of the lad, if perchance harm befalls the lad his father too will die — and this is what he said: ״והיה כראותו כי אין הנער ומת״ — 'and it will be, when he sees that the lad is gone, he will die.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:20:14.156096306Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}